  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">For questions 1 - 7, use the equation \(3x + 4y =12\)</para>
      <exercise id="_33ba9218-21e3-44a6-b162-ab42818b7db4" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Find the value of \(y\) when \(x = 0\).</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Correct! 3</para>
          <para id="para-00004">Nice try! The correct answer is 3.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="bdfae59e-ac64-4001-8c66-2ef317efcd04" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00005">Find the value of \(x\) when \(y = 0\).</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">Correct! 4</para>
          <para id="para-00007">Nice try! The correct answer is 4.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Q#3-->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00008">Plot both of those points on a coordinate grid and use a ruler to draw a line.</para>
          <para id="para-00009">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
          
            <media alt="A plot of the x and y coordiantes of the equation 3x + 4y =12.">
              <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_07_03_01.jpg"/>
            </media>
          
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q#4-->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00011">What is the coordinate of the \(x\)-intercept?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00012">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00013">\((4,0)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q#5-->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00014">What is the coordinate of the \(y\)-intercept?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00015">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00016">\((0,3)\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q#6-->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00017">What are two other names for the \(x\)-intercept?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00018">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00019">zero, solution</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <exercise id="_1d3b286b-14fe-4dc7-adb6-c892ead56130" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00020">What is the slope of the line?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00021">Correct! \(-\frac34\)</para>
          <para id="para-00022">Nice try! The correct answer is \(-\frac34\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
    <section id="sect-00002">
      <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
        <para id="para-00023">Graph the equation \(5x-2y= 10\). Which of the following describes the intercepts and slope of the graph?</para>
      </note>
    </section>
    <section id="sect-00003">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      <section id="sect-00004">
        <title>Graphing a Line and Describing Characteristics</title>
        <para id="para-00024">There are many ways to graph an equation of a line. One way is to use the \(x\)-intercepts and \(y\)-intercepts as two points on the line.</para>
        <section id="sect-00005">
          <title>Example</title>
          <para id="para-00025">Graph \(3x -6y =18\) using the intercepts, then identify key characteristics.</para>
          <para id="para-00026"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Find the \(x\)-intercept.<newline/> To find the \(x\)-intercept, let \(y=0\).</para>
          <para id="para-00027">\(\begin{array}{rcl}3x -6y &amp;=&amp;18\<newline/> \3x -6(0) &amp;=&amp;18\<newline/> \3x&amp;=&amp;18\<newline/> \x&amp;=&amp;6\end{array}\)</para>
          <para id="para-00028">\((6,0)\) is the \(x\)-intercept<newline/> The \(x\)-intercept is also called a solution or zero.</para>
          <para id="para-00029"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> -Find the \(y\)-intercept.<newline/> To find the \(y\)-intercept, let \(x=0\).</para>
          <para id="para-00030">\(\begin{array}{rcl}3x -6y &amp;=&amp;18\<newline/> \3(0) -6y &amp;=&amp;18\<newline/> \-6y &amp;=&amp;18\<newline/> \y&amp;=&amp;-3\end{array}\)</para>
          <para id="para-00031">\((0, -3)\) is the \(y\)-intercept</para>
          <para id="para-00032"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> -Graph the line by connecting the \(y\)-intercepts.</para>
          
            <media alt="A plot of y intercepts of the equation 3x - 6y =18.">
              <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_07_05_01.jpg"/>
            </media>
          
          <para id="para-00033"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Find the slope of the line.</para>
          <para id="para-00034">\(\mathrm{slope}=\frac{\mathrm{rise}}{\mathrm{run}}=\frac36=\frac12\)</para>
        </section>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
          <title>Try It: Graphing a Line and Describing Characteristics</title>
        <para id="para-00035">For 1 - 2, use the equation \(7x - 3y = 21\).</para>
          <!--Q#1-->

          <exercise id="exer-00005">
            <problem id="prob-00008">
              <para id="para-00036">Graph the equation using the intercepts.</para>
              <para id="para-00037">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00008">
              <para id="para-00038">Compare your answer:</para>
              <para id="para-00039">
                <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>
             </para>
              
                <media alt="Graph of the equation 7x - 3y = 21.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_07_05_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
              
            </solution>
          </exercise>
          <!--Interaction End -->

          <exercise id="_1ff5a0d5-9bb2-4cb3-af25-2a9d40b8fde3" class="multiple-choice">
            <problem id="prob-00009">
              <para id="para-00040">What is the slope of the line?</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00009">
              <para id="para-00041">Correct! \(\frac73\)</para>
              <para id="para-00042">Nice try! The correct answer is \(\frac73\).</para>
            </solution>
          </exercise>
        </note>
      </section>
    </section>
